module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Nagata.JapaneseCriteria
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.NormalLocus.Open

@[expose] public section

/-!
# N-1 for a Noetherian domain: normality on a dense open plus N-1 at every maximal ideal

Let `R` be a Noetherian domain with fraction field `K`. Proof of Tag 0333: `R` is N-1 if and only
if `R_f` is normal for some nonzero `f ∈ R` and `R_𝔪` is N-1 for every maximal ideal `𝔪`.

Necessity is cheap. The integral closure `R'` of `R` in `K` is a fractional ideal as soon as it is
a finite `R`-module — finitely many generators have a common denominator `f ≠ 0` — and `f R' ⊆ R`
says exactly that every element of `K` integral over `R` has an `f`-power multiple in `R`, which is
normality of `R_f`; and N-1 passes to localizations (Lemma 032G).

For the converse it suffices, by Lemma 032H, to exhibit for each maximal ideal `𝔪` an element
`g ∉ 𝔪` with `R_g` N-1: the set of such `g` generates the unit ideal, and N-1 descends along a
principal open cover. Fix `𝔪`. Condition (2) makes the integral closure of `R_𝔪` in `K` a finite
`R_𝔪`-module, and clearing denominators produces a *finite* `R`-subalgebra `B ⊆ K` — generated by
suitably scaled `R_𝔪`-module generators — with the property that every element of `K` integral
over `R` has an `R ∖ 𝔪`-multiple in `B`. That property, transported along `R → B`, makes `B_𝔮`
normal for every prime `𝔮` of `B` over `𝔪`, and it makes `B_f = R_f` normal, so Lemma 0332 applies
to `B`: the non-normal locus of `Spec(B)` is closed. Its vanishing ideal `J` meets `R` in an ideal
not contained in `𝔪`, because otherwise a prime of `B` over `𝔪` would contain `J`, hence be
non-normal. An element `g ∈ J ∩ R ∖ 𝔪` then lies in every prime of `B` containing the ideal of
denominators of a given `x ∈ K` integral over `R`, so a power of `g` multiplies `x` into `B`:
`R'_g = B_g` is a finite `R_g`-module and `R_g` is N-1.

## Implementation notes

*The denominator condition is `∃ m ∈ M, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (m • z)` throughout.* This is
the spelling of `IsFractional`, of `IsLocalization.exist_integer_multiples_of_finset` and of
`multiple_mem_span_of_mem_localization_span`, so those land with no glue; writing it as
`algebraMap B K m * z = algebraMap B K c` instead costs a `ring_nf` at every junction.

*Normality of a localization is a single iff.* `isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff` says that a
localization `T` of a domain `B` at a submonoid `M` of nonzerodivisors is integrally closed exactly
when every element of the fraction field integral over `B` has an `M`-multiple in `B`. Both
directions are used, at four different submonoids, and the lemma builds the `K`-algebra structure
on `T` internally, so no `Algebra T K` instance appears in a statement. Its transport up an
integral extension, `isIntegrallyClosed_localization_of_forall_exists_smul_mem`, is what turns the
one denominator bound coming out of condition (2) into normality of `B` at every prime over `𝔪`
and at `f` alike.

*The non-normal locus is not pushed forward to `Spec(R)`.* Instead the vanishing ideal `J` of the
closed set is contracted to `R`, and the two facts a closed image would provide are used
separately: lying over for the integral extension `R → B` shows `J ∩ R ⊄ 𝔪`, and membership of `g`
in every prime of the closed set turns into membership in the radical of the ideal of denominators
`(1 : Submodule B K).colon {x}`. This keeps the argument inside `Spec(B)`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0333](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0333)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Stacks.Nagata.NormalLocusCriterion

/-- N-1 over an arbitrary fraction field: `A` is N-1 exactly when the integral closure of `A` in
any ring of fractions `L` of `A` is a finite `A`-module. -/
private theorem isN1_iff_module_finite_integralClosure {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (L : Type*)
    [Field L] [Algebra A L] [IsFractionRing A L] :
    IsN1 A ↔ Module.Finite A (integralClosure A L) :=
  ⟨fun _ => Module.Finite.equiv (FractionRing.algEquiv A L).mapIntegralClosure.toLinearEquiv,
    fun _ => Module.Finite.equiv (FractionRing.algEquiv A L).mapIntegralClosure.symm.toLinearEquiv⟩

/-- A prime of `Spec(B)` lies in a closed set exactly when it contains the vanishing ideal of that
set. -/
private theorem mem_iff_vanishingIdeal_le {B : Type*} [CommRing B] {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum B)}
    (hZ : IsClosed Z) (q : PrimeSpectrum B) :
    q ∈ Z ↔ PrimeSpectrum.vanishingIdeal Z ≤ q.asIdeal := by
  refine ⟨fun hq _ hf => (PrimeSpectrum.mem_vanishingIdeal _ _).mp hf q hq, fun h => ?_⟩
  rw [← hZ.closure_eq, ← PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_vanishingIdeal_eq_closure]
  exact (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus _ _).mpr h

section Denominators

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {K : Type*} [CommRing K] [Algebra R K]

/-- An element of `M` acts invertibly on every `A`-submodule of `K`, `A` being the localization of
`R` at `M`: it is the image of a unit of `A`. -/
private theorem smul_mem_iff_of_mem (M : Submonoid R) (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    [IsLocalization M A] [Algebra A K] [IsScalarTower R A K] {m : R} (hm : m ∈ M)
    (N : Submodule A K) {x : K} : m • x ∈ N ↔ x ∈ N := by
  rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul A m x]
  exact N.smul_mem_iff_of_isUnit (IsLocalization.map_units A ⟨m, hm⟩)

/-- The integral closure of `A` in `K` is a finite `A`-module as soon as it is contained in some
finitely generated `A`-submodule of `K`, `A` being Noetherian. -/
private theorem module_finite_integralClosure_of_forall_mem {A : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [Algebra A K] {N : Submodule A K} (hN : N.FG)
    (h : ∀ x : K, IsIntegral A x → x ∈ N) : Module.Finite A (integralClosure A K) := by
  exact (Module.Finite.iff_fg (N := Subalgebra.toSubmodule (integralClosure A K))).mpr
    (hN.of_le fun x hx => h x hx)

/-- The `A`-span of the image of a module-finite `R`-algebra `B` in `K` is a finitely generated
`A`-module, for any `R`-algebra `A` mapping to `K`. -/
private theorem fg_span_range_algebraMap (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [Algebra A K] [Algebra R A]
    [IsScalarTower R A K] (B : Type*) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra B K]
    [IsScalarTower R B K] [Module.Finite R B] :
    (Submodule.span A (Set.range (algebraMap B K))).FG := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ : (⊤ : Submodule R B).FG := Module.finite_def.mp inferInstance
  refine ⟨u.image (algebraMap B K), ?_⟩
  rw [Finset.coe_image]
  refine le_antisymm (Submodule.span_mono (Set.image_subset_range _ _)) ?_
  rw [Submodule.span_le]
  rintro z ⟨b, rfl⟩
  have hb : b ∈ Submodule.span R (u : Set B) := hu ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  have hmap := Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (f := (Algebra.linearMap B K).restrictScalars R) hb
  rw [Submodule.map_span] at hmap
  exact Submodule.span_le_restrictScalars R A _ hmap

/-- **Generators integral over `R` with a denominator bound.** Let `A` be the localization of `R`
at `M` and suppose the integral closure of `A` in `K` is a finite `A`-module. Then there is a
finite set `s ⊆ K` of elements integral over `R` such that every element of `K` integral over `R`
has an `M`-multiple in the `R`-span of `s`.

Generators of the integral closure may be scaled by elements of `M` to become integral over `R`
without changing their `A`-span, the scalars being units in `A`. -/
private theorem exists_finset_isIntegral_forall_exists_smul_mem_span (M : Submonoid R)
    (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [IsLocalization M A] [Algebra A K]
    [IsScalarTower R A K] (hfin : Module.Finite A (integralClosure A K)) :
    ∃ s : Finset K, (∀ x ∈ s, IsIntegral R x) ∧
      ∀ z : K, IsIntegral R z → ∃ m ∈ M, m • z ∈ Submodule.span R (s : Set K) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s₀, hs₀⟩ : (Subalgebra.toSubmodule (integralClosure A K)).FG :=
    Module.Finite.iff_fg.mp hfin
  have hchoose : ∀ y ∈ s₀, ∃ m : M, IsIntegral R ((m : R) • y) := fun y hy =>
    IsIntegral.exists_multiple_integral_of_isLocalization M (Rₘ := A) y
      (show y ∈ Subalgebra.toSubmodule (integralClosure A K) from
        hs₀ ▸ Submodule.subset_span hy)
  choose d hd using hchoose
  set s : Finset K := s₀.attach.image fun p => (d p.1 p.2 : R) • p.1
  have hmems : ∀ y, ∀ hy : y ∈ s₀, (d y hy : R) • y ∈ s := fun y hy =>
    Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (s₀.mem_attach ⟨y, hy⟩)
  refine ⟨s, Finset.forall_mem_image.mpr fun p _ => hd p.1 p.2, fun z hz => ?_⟩
  have hle : Submodule.span A (s₀ : Set K) ≤ Submodule.span A (s : Set K) :=
    Submodule.span_le.mpr fun y hy =>
      (smul_mem_iff_of_mem M A (d y hy).2 _).mp (Submodule.subset_span (hmems y hy))
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := multiple_mem_span_of_mem_localization_span M A (s : Set K) z
    (hle (hs₀ ▸ hz.tower_top (A := A)))
  exact ⟨m, m.2, hm⟩

/-- A localization `T` of a domain `R` at a submonoid of nonzerodivisors is an `R`-compatible
algebra over the fraction field `K` of `R`, of which `K` is again the fraction field. -/
private theorem exists_algebra_isScalarTower_isFractionRing (M : Submonoid R)
    (hM : M ≤ nonZeroDivisors R) [IsFractionRing R K] (T : Type*) [CommRing T] [Algebra R T]
    [IsLocalization M T] :
    ∃ _ : Algebra T K, IsScalarTower R T K ∧ IsFractionRing T K := by
  let inst : Algebra T K := (IsLocalization.lift (M := M) (S := T) (g := algebraMap R K)
    (fun y => IsLocalization.map_units K ⟨(y : R), hM y.2⟩)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R T K :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (IsLocalization.lift_eq _ x).symm
  exact ⟨inst, this, IsFractionRing.isFractionRing_of_isLocalization M T K hM⟩

end Denominators

section Localization

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra B K]
  [IsFractionRing B K]

/-- **Normality of a localization, as a denominator condition.** A localization `T` of a domain `B`
at a submonoid `M` of nonzerodivisors is integrally closed if and only if every element of the
fraction field `K` integral over `B` has an `M`-multiple in `B`. -/
private theorem isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff (M : Submonoid B)
    (hM : M ≤ nonZeroDivisors B) (T : Type*) [CommRing T] [Algebra B T] [IsLocalization M T] :
    IsIntegrallyClosed T ↔
      ∀ z : K, IsIntegral B z → ∃ m ∈ M, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (m • z) := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, _⟩ := exists_algebra_isScalarTower_isFractionRing (K := K) M hM T
  have hspec : ∀ (c : B) (m : M), algebraMap T K (IsLocalization.mk' T c m) * algebraMap B K m
      = algebraMap B K c := fun c m => by
    have h := congrArg (algebraMap T K) (IsLocalization.mk'_spec T c m)
    rwa [map_mul, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply] at h
  constructor
  · intro hT z hz
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := IsIntegrallyClosed.isIntegral_iff.mp (hz.tower_top (A := T))
    obtain ⟨⟨c, m⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective M y
    exact ⟨(m : B), m.2, c, by rw [Algebra.smul_def, ← hy, mul_comm, hspec]⟩
  · intro h
    rw [isIntegrallyClosed_iff K]
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨m₀, hm₀⟩ := IsIntegral.exists_multiple_integral_of_isLocalization M (Rₘ := T) x hx
    obtain ⟨m, hm, c, hc⟩ := h ((m₀ : B) • x) hm₀
    have hd : (m : B) * (m₀ : B) ∈ M := M.mul_mem hm m₀.2
    have hne : algebraMap B K ((m : B) * (m₀ : B)) ≠ 0 :=
      (map_ne_zero_iff _ (IsFractionRing.injective B K)).mpr (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (hM hd))
    refine ⟨IsLocalization.mk' T c ⟨(m : B) * (m₀ : B), hd⟩, mul_right_cancel₀ hne ?_⟩
    rw [hspec, hc, smul_smul, Algebra.smul_def, map_mul]
    ring

/-- **Necessity of a normal principal open.** If the integral closure of a domain `B` in its
fraction field `K` is a finite `B`-module, then it is a fractional ideal: its finitely many
generators have a common denominator `b ≠ 0`, and then `B_b` is integrally closed. -/
private theorem exists_ne_zero_isIntegrallyClosed_away
    (hfin : Module.Finite B (integralClosure B K)) :
    ∃ b : B, b ≠ 0 ∧ IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.Away b) := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : (Subalgebra.toSubmodule (integralClosure B K)).FG :=
    Module.Finite.iff_fg.mp hfin
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := IsLocalization.exist_integer_multiples_of_finset (nonZeroDivisors B)
    (S := K) s
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hfrac⟩ : IsFractional (nonZeroDivisors B) (Submodule.span B (s : Set K)) :=
    FractionalIdeal.isFractional_span_iff.mpr ⟨c, c.2, hc⟩
  have hb0 : b ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hb
  exact ⟨b, hb0, (isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff (K := K) (Submonoid.powers b)
    (powers_le_nonZeroDivisors_of_noZeroDivisors hb0) _).mpr fun z hz =>
      ⟨b, Submonoid.mem_powers b, hfrac z (hs ▸ hz)⟩⟩

end Localization

section Crux

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra R K]
  [IsFractionRing R K]

omit [IsDomain R] [IsFractionRing R K] in
/-- **Transporting a denominator bound up an integral extension.** Let `R ⊆ B ⊆ K` with `B` a
domain integral over `R` and `K` the fraction field of both. If every element of `K` integral over
`R` has an `M`-multiple in `B`, then the localization of `B` at any submonoid `N` of
nonzerodivisors containing the image of `M` is integrally closed. -/
private theorem isIntegrallyClosed_localization_of_forall_exists_smul_mem {B : Type*} [CommRing B]
    [IsDomain B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra B K] [IsScalarTower R B K] [IsFractionRing B K]
    [Algebra.IsIntegral R B] {M : Submonoid R} {N : Submonoid B}
    (hMN : M.map (algebraMap R B) ≤ N) (hN : N ≤ nonZeroDivisors B)
    (T : Type*) [CommRing T] [Algebra B T] [IsLocalization N T]
    (h : ∀ z : K, IsIntegral R z → ∃ m ∈ M, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (m • z)) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed T := by
  refine (isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff (K := K) N hN T).mpr fun z hz => ?_
  obtain ⟨m, hm, c, hc⟩ := h z (isIntegral_trans z hz)
  refine ⟨algebraMap R B m, hMN ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩, c, ?_⟩
  rw [hc, Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R B K]

omit [IsDomain R] [IsFractionRing R K] in
/-- **Spreading out normality of a finite subextension.** Let `R ⊆ B ⊆ K` with `B` integral over
`R` and Noetherian, let `b ∈ B` be nonzero with `B_b` normal, and let `𝔪` be a maximal ideal of `R`
such that `B_𝔮` is normal for every prime `𝔮` of `B` over `𝔪`. Then there is `g ∈ R ∖ 𝔪` such that
a `g`-power multiple of any element of `K` integral over `R` lies in `B`; that is, `B_g` is the
integral closure of `R_g` in `K`.

The non-normal locus of `Spec(B)` is closed (Lemma 0332); `g` is any element of `R ∖ 𝔪` in its
vanishing ideal `J`, which exists by lying over, and it works because the ideal of denominators of
an element integral over `R` is contained in no prime off the non-normal locus, so `g` lies in the
radical of that ideal. -/
private theorem exists_notMem_forall_exists_pow_smul_mem {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [IsDomain B]
    [IsNoetherianRing B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra B K] [IsScalarTower R B K] [IsFractionRing B K]
    [Algebra.IsIntegral R B] {b : B} (hb : b ≠ 0)
    (hbic : IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.Away b)) (𝔪 : Ideal R) [𝔪.IsMaximal]
    (hgood : ∀ (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime], Ideal.comap (algebraMap R B) q = 𝔪 →
      IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    ∃ g : R, g ∉ 𝔪 ∧ ∀ x : K, IsIntegral R x →
      ∃ n : ℕ, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (g ^ n • x) := by
  classical
  have hJ := mem_iff_vanishingIdeal_le
    (PrimeSpectrum.isOpen_setOf_isIntegrallyClosed_atPrime hb hbic).isClosed_compl
  set J : Ideal B := PrimeSpectrum.vanishingIdeal
    {p : PrimeSpectrum B | IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)}ᶜ
  have hnot : ¬ Ideal.comap (algebraMap R B) J ≤ 𝔪 := fun hle => by
    obtain ⟨Q, hQJ, hQp, hQm⟩ := Ideal.exists_ideal_over_prime_of_isIntegral 𝔪 J hle
    exact (hJ ⟨Q, hQp⟩).mpr hQJ (@hgood Q hQp hQm)
  obtain ⟨g, hgJ, hgm⟩ := IsConcreteLE.not_le_iff_exists.mp hnot
  refine ⟨g, hgm, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  have hmem : ∀ c : B, c ∈ (1 : Submodule B K).colon {x} ↔ IsLocalization.IsInteger B (c • x) :=
    fun c => by
      rw [Submodule.mem_colon_singleton, Submodule.mem_one]
      exact Iff.rfl
  have hrad : algebraMap R B g ∈ ((1 : Submodule B K).colon {x}).radical := by
    rw [Ideal.radical_eq_sInf]
    refine Submodule.mem_sInf.mpr fun q hq => ?_
    obtain ⟨hIq, hqp⟩ := hq
    by_cases hic : IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.AtPrime q)
    · obtain ⟨m, hm, hint⟩ := (isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff (K := K)
        (Ideal.primeCompl q) (Ideal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors q)
        (Localization.AtPrime q)).mp hic x hx.tower_top
      exact absurd (hIq ((hmem m).mpr hint)) hm
    · exact (hJ ⟨q, hqp⟩).mp hic (Ideal.mem_comap.mp hgJ)
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mp hrad
  have hint := (hmem _).mp hn
  rw [← map_pow, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul B (g ^ n) x] at hint
  exact ⟨n, hint⟩

variable [IsNoetherianRing R]

/-- **From a spread-out finite extension to N-1 on a principal open.** If `B` is a module-finite
`R`-subalgebra of `K` and a power of `g ≠ 0` multiplies every element of `K` integral over `R` into
`B`, then `R_g` is N-1. -/
private theorem isN1_away_of_forall_exists_pow_smul_mem
    (B : Type*) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra B K] [IsScalarTower R B K]
    [Module.Finite R B] {g : R} (hg : g ≠ 0)
    (h : ∀ x : K, IsIntegral R x → ∃ n : ℕ, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (g ^ n • x)) :
    IsN1 (Localization.Away g) := by
  have hM : Submonoid.powers g ≤ nonZeroDivisors R :=
    powers_le_nonZeroDivisors_of_noZeroDivisors hg
  obtain ⟨_, _, _⟩ := exists_algebra_isScalarTower_isFractionRing (K := K) _ hM
    (Localization.Away g)
  have : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.Away g) :=
    IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing (Submonoid.powers g) _ inferInstance
  rw [isN1_iff_module_finite_integralClosure (A := Localization.Away g) K]
  refine module_finite_integralClosure_of_forall_mem
    (fg_span_range_algebraMap (R := R) (Localization.Away g) B) fun x hx => ?_
  obtain ⟨m₀, hm₀⟩ := IsIntegral.exists_multiple_integral_of_isLocalization
    (Submonoid.powers g) (Rₘ := Localization.Away g) x hx
  obtain ⟨n, c, hc⟩ := h ((m₀ : R) • x) hm₀
  refine (smul_mem_iff_of_mem (Submonoid.powers g) (Localization.Away g)
    (Submonoid.mul_mem _ ⟨n, rfl⟩ m₀.2) _).mp ?_
  rw [show (g ^ n * (m₀ : R)) • x = algebraMap B K c by rw [hc, smul_smul]]
  exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨c, rfl⟩

/-- **The converse, at one maximal ideal.** Let `B` be a module-finite `R`-subalgebra of `K` with
`K` as its fraction field, let `f ≠ 0` have `R_f` normal, and suppose every element of `K`
integral over `R` has an `R ∖ 𝔪`-multiple in `B`. Then some `g ∉ 𝔪` has `R_g` N-1. -/
private theorem exists_notMem_isN1_away (B : Type*) [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra R B]
    [Algebra B K] [IsScalarTower R B K] [IsFractionRing B K] [Module.Finite R B]
    (𝔪 : Ideal R) [𝔪.IsMaximal] {f : R} (hf : f ≠ 0)
    (hfic : IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.Away f))
    (hden : ∀ z : K, IsIntegral R z →
      ∃ m ∈ 𝔪.primeCompl, IsLocalization.IsInteger B (m • z)) :
    ∃ g : R, g ∉ 𝔪 ∧ IsN1 (Localization.Away g) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing B := IsNoetherianRing.of_finite R B
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral R B := Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite R B
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R B) := fun x y hxy => by
    have h := congrArg (algebraMap B K) hxy
    rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply] at h
    exact IsFractionRing.injective R K h
  have hb0 : algebraMap R B f ≠ 0 := (map_ne_zero_iff _ hinj).mpr hf
  have hbic : IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.Away (algebraMap R B f)) :=
    isIntegrallyClosed_localization_of_forall_exists_smul_mem (K := K)
      (Submonoid.map_powers (algebraMap R B) f).le
      (powers_le_nonZeroDivisors_of_noZeroDivisors hb0) _ fun z hz => by
        obtain ⟨m, hm, c, hc⟩ := (isIntegrallyClosed_localization_iff (K := K)
          (Submonoid.powers f) (powers_le_nonZeroDivisors_of_noZeroDivisors hf)
          (Localization.Away f)).mp hfic z hz
        exact ⟨m, hm, algebraMap R B c, by rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply, hc]⟩
  have hgood : ∀ (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime], Ideal.comap (algebraMap R B) q = 𝔪 →
      IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.AtPrime q) := fun q _ hqm =>
    isIntegrallyClosed_localization_of_forall_exists_smul_mem (K := K)
      (by rintro y ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩; exact fun hy => hm (hqm ▸ Ideal.mem_comap.mpr hy))
      (Ideal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors q) _ hden
  obtain ⟨g, hgm, hg⟩ := exists_notMem_forall_exists_pow_smul_mem (K := K) hb0 hbic 𝔪 hgood
  exact ⟨g, hgm, isN1_away_of_forall_exists_pow_smul_mem B
    (fun h => hgm (h ▸ 𝔪.zero_mem)) hg⟩

end Crux

/-- **Stacks Tag 0333.** A Noetherian domain `R` is N-1 if and only if `R_f` is normal for some
nonzero `f ∈ R` and `R_𝔪` is N-1 for every maximal ideal `𝔪 ⊆ R`. -/
public theorem solution (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    IsN1 R ↔
      (∃ f : R, f ≠ 0 ∧ IsIntegrallyClosed (Localization.Away f)) ∧
        ∀ (𝔪 : Ideal R) [𝔪.IsMaximal], IsN1 (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪) := by
  refine ⟨fun hN1 => ⟨exists_ne_zero_isIntegrallyClosed_away (K := FractionRing R)
      ((isN1_iff_module_finite_integralClosure (FractionRing R)).mp hN1),
    fun 𝔪 _ => (isN1_and_isJapaneseRing_of_isLocalization 𝔪.primeCompl
      (Rₛ := Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)).1 hN1⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨⟨f, hf, hfic⟩, hloc⟩
  have key : ∀ (𝔪 : Ideal R) [𝔪.IsMaximal], ∃ g : R, g ∉ 𝔪 ∧ IsN1 (Localization.Away g) := by
    intro 𝔪 _
    obtain ⟨s, hsint, hsden⟩ := exists_finset_isIntegral_forall_exists_smul_mem_span
      (K := FractionRing R) 𝔪.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)
      ((isN1_iff_module_finite_integralClosure (FractionRing R)).mp (hloc 𝔪))
    have : Module.Finite R (Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set (FractionRing R))) :=
      Algebra.finite_adjoin_of_finite_of_isIntegral s.finite_toSet hsint
    refine exists_notMem_isN1_away (K := FractionRing R)
      (Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set (FractionRing R))) 𝔪 hf hfic fun z hz => ?_
    obtain ⟨m, hm, hmem⟩ := hsden z hz
    have hsub : Submodule.span R (s : Set (FractionRing R)) ≤
        Subalgebra.toSubmodule (Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set (FractionRing R))) :=
      Submodule.span_le.mpr Algebra.subset_adjoin
    exact ⟨m, hm, ⟨m • z, hsub hmem⟩, rfl⟩
  have hspan : Ideal.span {g : R | g ≠ 0 ∧ IsN1 (Localization.Away g)} = ⊤ := by
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨𝔪, h𝔪, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hne
    obtain ⟨g, hgm, hgN⟩ := @key 𝔪 h𝔪
    exact hgm (hle (Ideal.subset_span ⟨fun h => hgm (h ▸ 𝔪.zero_mem), hgN⟩))
  have : ∀ g : ({g : R | g ≠ 0 ∧ IsN1 (Localization.Away g)} : Set R),
      IsDomain (Localization.Away (g : R)) := fun g => Localization.Away.isDomain g.2.1
  exact (isN1_and_isJapaneseRing_of_localizationSpan _ hspan
    (Rₚ := fun g => Localization.Away (g : R))).1 fun g => g.2.2

end Stacks.Nagata.NormalLocusCriterion

end

/-!
# N-1 for a Noetherian domain is normality on a dense open plus N-1 at every maximal ideal

Let `R` be a Noetherian domain with field of fractions `K`, and let `R'` be the integral closure
of `R` in `K`. Then `R` is N-1 — that is, `R'` is a finite `R`-module (Definition 032F (1)) — if
and only if

1. there is a nonzero `f ∈ R` with `R_f` normal, and
2. `R_𝔪` is N-1 for every maximal ideal `𝔪 ⊆ R`.

Both conditions are necessary for a cheap reason. Finitely many `R`-module generators of `R'` are
fractions, so a single nonzero common denominator `f` has `R_f = R'_f`, which is normal; and N-1
passes to localizations (Lemma 032G), which gives (2) at every maximal ideal at once.

The content is the converse, and the two conditions enter it in different ways. Condition (1)
makes the non-normal locus of *any* finite extension `R ⊆ R' ⊆ K` a closed subset of `Spec(R')`
(Lemma 0332, applied to `R'`, which has the same localization at `f`), and its image `Z_{R'}` in
`Spec(R)` is closed because `Spec(R') → Spec(R)` is a closed map. Condition (2) produces, for each
maximal ideal `𝔪`, a finite extension `R' = R[x₁, …, x_n]` with `𝔪 ∉ Z_{R'}`: the integral closure
of `R_𝔪` in `K` is a finite `R_𝔪`-module, and its generators may be taken integral over `R`
(Lemma 0307). As `Spec(R)` is quasi-compact, finitely many such `R'_i` have `⋂ Z_{R'_i} = ∅`, and
the subring of `K` they generate is a finite extension of `R` that is normal at every prime, hence
normal, hence equal to `R'`.

## Main results

* `isN1_iff_exists_isIntegrallyClosed_away_and_forall_isN1_atPrime`: the equivalence, Tag 0333.

## Implementation notes

*Normality of a domain is `IsIntegrallyClosed`.* The source's "`R_f` is normal" is normality of a
ring (Definition 00GV: every localization at a prime is a normal domain), but `f ≠ 0` makes
`Localization.Away f` a domain (`Localization.Away.isDomain`), and for a domain that condition is
integral closedness in the field of fractions. `IsIntegrallyClosed` is how Mathlib says that, and
for a domain the two readings of "normal" agree in both directions — one way is
`IsIntegrallyClosed.of_localization_maximal`, the other that a localization of an integrally closed
domain is integrally closed. Noetherianness plays no part in that translation.

*The localizations are the concrete models `Localization.Away f` and `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪`.*
Both conditions are invariant under `R`-algebra isomorphism, so reading condition (1) at an
abstract `Rf` with `[IsLocalization.Away f Rf]`, or condition (2) at an `Rₘ` with
`[IsLocalization.AtPrime Rₘ 𝔪]`, is a transport along `IsLocalization.algEquiv`. This follows
Mathlib, whose localize-at-maximal-ideals statements — `IsIntegrallyClosed.of_localization_maximal`
is the one nearest this lemma — are phrased with `Localization.AtPrime` as well, and it keeps the
right-hand side free of quantification over models.

*`𝔪` carries `[𝔪.IsMaximal]` as an instance binder* so that `IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)`
is found by instance search (`IsLocalization.isDomain_of_local_atPrime`), `IsN1` being a predicate
on domains.

Faithfulness.
1. Every hypothesis is used by the conclusion: `[IsDomain R]` is what gives `R` a field of
   fractions, without which N-1 is not defined, and `[IsNoetherianRing R]` is used by the
   implication (1) ∧ (2) ⇒ N-1, through Lemma 0332 and the finiteness of the set of associated
   primes of `R/fR` behind it. The implication N-1 ⇒ (1) ∧ (2) uses no Noetherian hypothesis at all
   (Lemma 032G holds for any domain), so that hypothesis is carried by the equivalence rather than
   by both of its halves; it is the source's, and it is not dead.
2. The scalars and base are the source's: `IsN1 R` asserts finiteness over `R` of the integral
   closure of `R` in `Frac R`, and `IsN1 (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)` finiteness over `R_𝔪` of the
   integral closure of `R_𝔪` in `Frac(R_𝔪)`, the latter being the source's `K` since `R_𝔪` is a
   localization of the domain `R` inside `K`.
3. The maps are pinned, not merely assumed to exist: `Localization.Away f` and
   `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪` carry their canonical `R`-algebra structures, so the rings of the
   statement are the source's `R_f` and `R_𝔪`, not abstract rings with the same properties; and
   the integral closures are taken along those structure maps.
4. The instantiation is not degenerate: `ℤ`, and any Dedekind domain, satisfies all three
   conditions — N-1 because it is already integrally closed, (1) with `f = 1`, and (2) because a
   localization of a normal domain is normal — and no side of the equivalence is vacuous, since
   `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪` is a domain and not the zero ring. Neither conjunct is redundant in
   the argument: (1) is what makes the non-normal locus of a finite subextension closed, and (2)
   is what produces a subextension avoiding a given maximal ideal.

